Unsupervised Algorithm: Hierarchical Clustering
----------------------------------------------

To check which group the data belongs to

There are two types of hierarchical clustering
1. Agglomerative (Bottom up) technique
2. Divisive (Top down) technique

Note: Both uses distance between the cluster technique

Mechanism by which the data clusters is Linkage mechanism
Here Each of the data becomes cluster by itself

Agglomerative (Bottom up) technique:
1. Every point will be considered as its own cluster
2. Each cluster then merges with most similar cluster in a iterative way
3. This formation happens till single cluster is formed (we will limit the number of clusters needed)

Flow:
1. Distance metric:
The method for calculating the similarity between clusters is distance based

2. The linkage criteria:
This is rule for determining the distance between two groups of datapoints

Note: Output for the same can be visualised via Dendrogram

Flow Steps:
Step1: Each data point has a individual cluster
Dhoni, Ashwin, Rohit, Kohli, DK, Ritu, Bumrah, Siraj, Malinga

Note: Each and every player is a individual cluster. Totally 9 clusters for now

Step2: Each cluster will be calculated by its distance
CSk,   CSK     MI     RCB    RCB  CSK    MI      RCB   MI
Dhoni, Ashwin, Rohit, Kohli, DK, Ritu, Bumrah, Siraj, Malinga

Step3: 2 closest cluster based on the linkage will be merged into Single cluster

Step4: Again cluster will be calculated for this cluster
Example:
CSk,   CSK     MI     RCB    RCB  CSK    MI      RCB   MI
Dhoni, Ashwin, Rohit, Kohli, DK, Ritu, Bumrah, Siraj, Malinga

Farthest:
[CSK           ],  CSK,     [MI,           ]  RCB,    RCB,   MI ,     RCB
[Dhoni, Ritu   ]   Ashwin   [Rohit, Malinga]  Kholi,  DK     Bumrah   Siraj


With each iteration, to form a single cluster
Ritu moves near Dhoni
Malinga moves near Rohit
Siraj moves to Kohli

Types of Linkage:
1. Single - uses the shortest distance between the two points
2. Complete - uses the farthest/maximum distance between the two points
3. Average - uses the average distance between the two points and merges the closest the points
4. Ward method - It is to reduce the cluster variance
(wards form to reduce the variance within the cluster group)